<title>DUBAI: Eid starts on Saturday in five Gulf Arab states.</title>
<headline>Eid starts on Saturday in five Gulf Arab states.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Moslems in five Gulf Arab states will celebrate the start of the Eid al-Fitr feast on Saturday, marking the end of the fasting month of Ramadan.</p>
<p>Official media in the United Arab Emirates, Bahrain, Kuwait, Qatar and Saudi Arabia, said on Friday the new moon which marks the end of Ramadan was sighted and the Eid would start on Saturday.</p>
<p>In Oman the Eid starts on Sunday, the Omani news agency ONA said.</p>
<p>The public holiday lasts five days in Saudi Arabia and three days in the other countries.</p>
</text>
